<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch11-techniques-of-integration">
  <title>Techniques of Integration</title>
  <shorttitle>Integration Techniques</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>Different integrands require different methods. Substitution reverses the chain rule, integration by parts reverses the product rule, and identities or partial fractions simplify the expression before integration. We will also treat improper integrals as limits and distinguish convergence from the availability of an elementary antiderivative.</p></introduction>

